    "introduction": "Alejandra Flores has appeared in dozens of theatrical productions, in lead and supporting roles. She has worked with the Cornerstone Theatre Company, the Center Theatre Group at the Mark Taper Forum, Bilingual Foundation of the Arts, Cal State University and others. She received a Cesar Award as a supporting actress, and a Drama-Logue Award for Outstanding Achievement in Theater. She has directed major theatrical productions including \"Too Many Tamales\", :Blood Wedding\" and others. She has hosted and produced radio shows. Her film credits include: Coyote (2013), Friends with Money (2006), A Walk in the Clouds (1995). Her TV credits include: ER, Sons of Anarchy, Prime Suspect, Switched at Birth, Southland, Nip/Tuck, Brothers and Sisters, The Shield, The Guardian and others. She had a recurring role in The Bold and the Beautiful (2002-2004) on CBS.Alejandra has a Bachelor of Arts Degree (National University of Mexico). She is the recipient of the Artist-in-Residence (AIR). She is the founder and director of the Los Angeles Theatre Academy.",
